WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.573
- I actually don't know where to start.

00:00:04.180 --> 00:00:07.280
I'm just, I'm so furious.

00:00:07.280 --> 00:00:09.653
And I'm so sad for our country.

00:00:13.760 --> 00:00:17.410
That they claim to be the
party of law and order.

00:00:17.410 --> 00:00:20.830
The hypocrisy makes it
feel like ash in my mouth

00:00:20.830 --> 00:00:22.310
to even say it.

00:00:22.310 --> 00:00:26.140
Because there's no depth, no illegality

00:00:26.140 --> 00:00:28.923
to which the president will not stoop.

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:32.003
It's astounding.

00:00:38.230 --> 00:00:42.180
The president has completed
what appears to be

00:00:42.180 --> 00:00:47.180
the first raft of pardons
in the lame-duck period.

00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:51.863
It's a murderers' row of the unpardonable.

00:00:52.870 --> 00:00:55.030
Though, an actual row of murderers

00:00:55.030 --> 00:00:57.820
are probably less morally blameworthy

00:00:57.820 --> 00:00:59.940
than the people that actually
received the pardons.

00:00:59.940 --> 00:01:01.940
Actual war criminals

00:01:01.940 --> 00:01:05.170
who were responsible for
killing innocent Iraqi citizens,

00:01:05.170 --> 00:01:06.750
including women and children.

00:01:06.750 --> 00:01:08.730
Ridiculously corrupt politicians,

00:01:08.730 --> 00:01:10.700
like Chris Collins and Duncan Hunter,

00:01:10.700 --> 00:01:12.000
who were convicted of

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:15.120
and were about to serve
extensive prison sentences

00:01:15.120 --> 00:01:17.610
related to insider trading

00:01:17.610 --> 00:01:20.540
and also embezzling campaign funds.

00:01:20.540 --> 00:01:21.850
Including, but not limited to,

00:01:21.850 --> 00:01:23.630
spending those campaign funds

00:01:23.630 --> 00:01:25.760
on extramarital affairs.

00:01:25.760 --> 00:01:28.420
Actual traitors to this country

00:01:28.420 --> 00:01:29.980
like Paul Manafort,

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:32.190
who was a direct conduit to the Russians

00:01:32.190 --> 00:01:34.883
through Konstantin Kilimnik
and Oleg Deripaska.

00:01:35.950 --> 00:01:38.230
And, of course, the president's cronies.

00:01:38.230 --> 00:01:40.510
Including, but not
limited to, Paul Manafort.

00:01:40.510 --> 00:01:43.383
But also Roger Stone
and George Papadopoulos.

00:01:44.870 --> 00:01:47.863
There's just no end to the depravity.

00:01:49.010 --> 00:01:53.470
This is unprecedented in its
baseness, in its venality.

00:01:53.470 --> 00:01:55.060
We've just never seen anything

00:01:55.060 --> 00:01:56.623
like this in the US.

00:01:57.820 --> 00:02:00.810
Effectively, every significant defendant

00:02:00.810 --> 00:02:02.660
who refused to cooperate with

00:02:02.660 --> 00:02:03.940
both the Mueller Investigation

00:02:03.940 --> 00:02:06.690
and also just Main Justice

00:02:06.690 --> 00:02:07.760
have now been pardoned.

00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:10.600
The only exceptions being
Rick Gates and Michael Cohen,

00:02:10.600 --> 00:02:12.750
both of whom actually testified

00:02:12.750 --> 00:02:15.430
and cooperated against the president.

00:02:15.430 --> 00:02:17.550
And this is tinpot, dictator,

00:02:17.550 --> 00:02:19.740
Banana Republic level corruption.

00:02:19.740 --> 00:02:23.770
If this seems like comic book villainy,

00:02:23.770 --> 00:02:25.610
that's because it is.

00:02:25.610 --> 00:02:27.580
This is not a close case.

00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:30.410
This is not an issue of red versus blue.

00:02:30.410 --> 00:02:33.463
This is just pure, flat out corruption.

00:02:34.450 --> 00:02:37.260
And, I guess, let's
start with the bad news

00:02:37.260 --> 00:02:39.440
because on some levels

00:02:39.440 --> 00:02:41.530
this is worse than it appears.

00:02:41.530 --> 00:02:45.500
It's not just that the
morally reprehensible

00:02:45.500 --> 00:02:49.980
and actual criminals have been pardoned.

00:02:49.980 --> 00:02:51.740
It's that this threatens

00:02:51.740 --> 00:02:55.750
the very fabric of our justice system.

00:02:55.750 --> 00:02:58.390
In part, because this
is just the opening act.

00:02:58.390 --> 00:02:59.980
There's no reason to think

00:02:59.980 --> 00:03:00.813
that President Trump

00:03:00.813 --> 00:03:03.170
is going to stop with these pardons.

00:03:03.170 --> 00:03:05.630
In fact, there's very good reason to think

00:03:05.630 --> 00:03:10.343
that this is just out
there to get people tired.

00:03:10.343 --> 00:03:12.970
That the worst pardons are yet to come.

00:03:12.970 --> 00:03:14.620
And it's the usual suspects

00:03:14.620 --> 00:03:16.630
who are the obvious candidates here.

00:03:16.630 --> 00:03:18.450
There's no reason to
think that the president

00:03:18.450 --> 00:03:22.170
will refrain from pardoning Jared Kushner;

00:03:22.170 --> 00:03:23.340
pardoning Bill Barr;

00:03:23.340 --> 00:03:28.340
pardoning himself, Ivanka, Don Junior;

00:03:28.360 --> 00:03:32.230
Allen Weisselberg, the CFO
of the Trump Organization.

00:03:32.230 --> 00:03:36.620
But President Trump
doesn't have those lines.

00:03:36.620 --> 00:03:38.270
He doesn't feel shame.

00:03:38.270 --> 00:03:42.690
And he doesn't give a damn
about political norms.

00:03:42.690 --> 00:03:43.850
Because what happened here

00:03:43.850 --> 00:03:45.470
is a really, really big deal.

00:03:45.470 --> 00:03:46.610
President Trump is pardoning

00:03:46.610 --> 00:03:47.460
a whole bunch of people

00:03:47.460 --> 00:03:50.320
who engaged in criminality in furtherance

00:03:50.320 --> 00:03:52.350
of the president's own agenda.

00:03:52.350 --> 00:03:53.970
For his own campaign.

00:03:53.970 --> 00:03:54.930
And for other reasons

00:03:54.930 --> 00:03:57.740
that benefit President Trump personally.

00:03:57.740 --> 00:03:59.850
Because the problem with pardoning people

00:03:59.850 --> 00:04:01.690
who engage in actual criminality

00:04:01.690 --> 00:04:03.510
for the benefit of the sitting president,

00:04:03.510 --> 00:04:04.830
if the president is allowed

00:04:04.830 --> 00:04:07.960
to pardon and absolve
guilt after the fact,

00:04:07.960 --> 00:04:09.180
there's a million ways

00:04:09.180 --> 00:04:11.200
for a sitting president to grift that.

00:04:11.200 --> 00:04:12.450
Let's take an extreme example.

00:04:12.450 --> 00:04:13.283
We all often talk about

00:04:13.283 --> 00:04:14.810
how the president could kill

00:04:14.810 --> 00:04:16.350
someone on Fifth Avenue,

00:04:16.350 --> 00:04:17.980
but what if the president hired someone

00:04:17.980 --> 00:04:19.970
to kill a political opponent

00:04:19.970 --> 00:04:21.760
and then decided to pardon them.

00:04:21.760 --> 00:04:23.070
Or a less extreme example.

00:04:23.070 --> 00:04:24.640
Let's call it stochastic terrorism,

00:04:24.640 --> 00:04:25.473
where the president just says,

00:04:25.473 --> 00:04:26.767
"Hey, it'd be really great

00:04:26.767 --> 00:04:29.200
"if someone killed my
main political rival."

00:04:29.200 --> 00:04:31.870
And then if you actually
pardon that person,

00:04:31.870 --> 00:04:34.630
which potentially the president could do,

00:04:34.630 --> 00:04:36.440
well, then it just incentivizes

00:04:36.440 --> 00:04:38.480
actual murder of political opponents.

00:04:38.480 --> 00:04:40.690
And while that's obviously extreme,

00:04:40.690 --> 00:04:42.810
Vladimir Putin has I tried this twice

00:04:42.810 --> 00:04:45.780
with his main political
rival, Alexei Navalny.

00:04:45.780 --> 00:04:48.160
And, obviously, there's
a state law issue here.

00:04:48.160 --> 00:04:50.010
Murder is generally a state law crime.

00:04:50.010 --> 00:04:51.370
So maybe the pardon wouldn't work,

00:04:51.370 --> 00:04:52.600
but how about this.

00:04:52.600 --> 00:04:55.640
What if the president
intentionally engaged

00:04:55.640 --> 00:04:59.100
in all kinds of campaign
finance violations?

00:04:59.100 --> 00:05:01.240
Getting, let's say, billions of dollars

00:05:01.240 --> 00:05:02.750
for a campaign slush fund

00:05:02.750 --> 00:05:04.310
and then just pardoned all the people

00:05:04.310 --> 00:05:06.890
who engaged in campaign finance violations

00:05:06.890 --> 00:05:08.950
for the benefit of the sitting president,

00:05:08.950 --> 00:05:10.240
who would then have the benefit

00:05:10.240 --> 00:05:13.810
of billions of dollars of campaign funds.

00:05:13.810 --> 00:05:16.270
If the president can
pardon co-conspirators

00:05:16.270 --> 00:05:18.210
or pardon those who engage in criminality

00:05:18.210 --> 00:05:19.390
at the president's benefit,

00:05:19.390 --> 00:05:21.610
or just simply hand out pardons

00:05:21.610 --> 00:05:22.950
like Thank You cards,

00:05:22.950 --> 00:05:25.870
there is no end to gaming the system.

00:05:25.870 --> 00:05:28.280
And, of course, on the
other side of the aisle,

00:05:28.280 --> 00:05:32.330
so far the Republicans have
been absolutely silent.

00:05:32.330 --> 00:05:35.674
Those people who will jump over themselves

00:05:35.674 --> 00:05:38.350
to fawn over this president.

00:05:38.350 --> 00:05:40.660
Ben Shapiro, Mark Levin, Tucker Carlson

00:05:40.660 --> 00:05:42.223
have said absolutely nothing.

00:05:43.230 --> 00:05:44.063
Nothing.

00:05:45.170 --> 00:05:46.003
And like I said,

00:05:46.003 --> 00:05:46.860
this isn't a close case.

00:05:46.860 --> 00:05:49.475
This is not my side versus yours.

00:05:49.475 --> 00:05:53.750
This isn't an affront to
the actual rule of law.

00:05:53.750 --> 00:05:54.750
Really, at this point,

00:05:54.750 --> 00:05:57.620
only Ben Sasse has had the temerity

00:05:57.620 --> 00:05:59.340
to even criticize the move

00:05:59.340 --> 00:06:01.940
saying that "this is rotten to the core."

00:06:01.940 --> 00:06:03.000
Well, gee.

00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:04.130
Thanks, Ben.

00:06:04.130 --> 00:06:05.483
Thank you for your service.

00:06:06.710 --> 00:06:08.430
And by backing those words up

00:06:08.430 --> 00:06:11.113
with absolutely no action whatsoever.

00:06:12.150 --> 00:06:13.330
Because there's a lot of damage

00:06:13.330 --> 00:06:15.740
that's actually going to keep happening

00:06:15.740 --> 00:06:17.900
before January 20th gets here.

00:06:17.900 --> 00:06:20.130
And there is absolutely nothing

00:06:20.130 --> 00:06:23.040
that's in the works to try and stop this.

00:06:23.040 --> 00:06:25.190
But I shouldn't criticize Ben Sasse.

00:06:25.190 --> 00:06:27.540
At least he came forward publicly

00:06:27.540 --> 00:06:29.920
and at least criticized the president.

00:06:29.920 --> 00:06:33.170
Everybody else seems to be happy

00:06:33.170 --> 00:06:35.793
just to sit idly by and silent.

00:06:38.190 --> 00:06:39.890
And, unfortunately, it gets worse.

00:06:41.020 --> 00:06:45.300
Contrary to what you might
read on Facebook or Twitter,

00:06:45.300 --> 00:06:46.880
Trump is almost certainly not going

00:06:46.880 --> 00:06:48.060
to face criminal scrutiny

00:06:48.060 --> 00:06:50.570
for even pardoning Manafort or Stone,

00:06:50.570 --> 00:06:51.763
or anybody else.

00:06:53.640 --> 00:06:56.120
Absent actual evidence

00:06:56.120 --> 00:06:59.059
that there was an explicit quid pro quo

00:06:59.059 --> 00:07:02.863
between Trump and his co-conspirators,

00:07:06.030 --> 00:07:08.620
there's not going to be
criminal repercussions.

00:07:08.620 --> 00:07:09.720
There's just not.

00:07:09.720 --> 00:07:12.690
And I don't think even

00:07:12.690 --> 00:07:14.681
an aggressive attorney general

00:07:14.681 --> 00:07:16.080
in the next administration

00:07:16.080 --> 00:07:16.960
is going to change that.

00:07:16.960 --> 00:07:18.193
It's an abuse of power.

00:07:20.290 --> 00:07:21.963
The guardrail is impeachment.

00:07:23.611 --> 00:07:26.220
And when you have a couple of days left

00:07:26.220 --> 00:07:27.260
in the Trump presidency,

00:07:27.260 --> 00:07:30.200
impeachment is no real
guardrail whatsoever.

00:07:30.200 --> 00:07:32.820
So for all intents and purposes,

00:07:32.820 --> 00:07:34.730
it's unlikely that President Trump

00:07:34.730 --> 00:07:36.270
is going to face any kind of

00:07:36.270 --> 00:07:39.800
real scrutiny as a
result of these actions.

00:07:39.800 --> 00:07:42.370
And while these are uncharted waters,

00:07:42.370 --> 00:07:46.070
absent very strong proof
of a separate crime

00:07:46.070 --> 00:07:49.203
like extortion or bribery,

00:07:50.160 --> 00:07:52.440
these pardons are not going
to be declared illegal.

00:07:52.440 --> 00:07:53.273
And it's not even clear

00:07:53.273 --> 00:07:55.070
that if you found this
separate criminality

00:07:55.070 --> 00:07:57.080
that it could be declared illegal.

00:07:57.080 --> 00:07:58.480
The parties themselves.

00:07:58.480 --> 00:08:01.290
And don't expect future state or federal

00:08:01.290 --> 00:08:03.450
prosecutions of Manafort or Stone.

00:08:03.450 --> 00:08:06.590
The complications are
probably grave enough

00:08:06.590 --> 00:08:09.160
that it's unlikely that they're going

00:08:09.160 --> 00:08:12.620
to face punishment for
their actual crimes.

00:08:12.620 --> 00:08:14.160
And, like I said,

00:08:14.160 --> 00:08:15.800
the pardons will continue.

00:08:15.800 --> 00:08:17.548
The message has been sent that

00:08:17.548 --> 00:08:20.960
if you uphold your silence

00:08:20.960 --> 00:08:24.823
against who is effectively a mafia don,

00:08:26.580 --> 00:08:28.053
you're going to get a pardon.

00:08:29.040 --> 00:08:31.290
You will be rewarded for your service

00:08:31.290 --> 00:08:33.580
and contravention of justice.

00:08:33.580 --> 00:08:35.393
There's no real silver lining there.

00:08:36.550 --> 00:08:37.840
That die is cast.

00:08:37.840 --> 00:08:39.860
That norm has been broken

00:08:39.860 --> 00:08:43.790
and you can expect that
future administrations

00:08:43.790 --> 00:08:45.140
are going to take note

00:08:45.140 --> 00:08:47.130
if there are no real penalties

00:08:47.130 --> 00:08:49.690
for abusing the pardon power this way.

00:08:49.690 --> 00:08:51.380
And it's ironic, too.

00:08:51.380 --> 00:08:52.980
Because, traditionally, the pardon power

00:08:52.980 --> 00:08:56.270
has been grossly underused.

00:08:56.270 --> 00:08:58.820
There are thousands of people who receive

00:08:58.820 --> 00:09:02.483
grossly inappropriate
sentences every year.

00:09:04.200 --> 00:09:06.680
For all the good that
the justice system does,

00:09:06.680 --> 00:09:08.530
it does a lot of bad too.

00:09:08.530 --> 00:09:11.890
Or at least it's often overzealous

00:09:11.890 --> 00:09:13.550
in punishing crimes.

00:09:13.550 --> 00:09:15.410
And there are a lot of
people who are in jail

00:09:15.410 --> 00:09:17.350
that, arguably, should not be.

00:09:17.350 --> 00:09:20.320
And, historically, presidents
are much more likely

00:09:20.320 --> 00:09:22.180
to underuse the pardon power

00:09:22.180 --> 00:09:24.960
than they are to overuse it.

00:09:24.960 --> 00:09:27.870
And to date, we've never seen anything

00:09:27.870 --> 00:09:30.470
like what President Trump has done.

00:09:30.470 --> 00:09:32.920
But the whataboutism is strong.

00:09:32.920 --> 00:09:34.850
People have pointed to the pardoning

00:09:34.850 --> 00:09:37.460
of Marc Rich by President Clinton

00:09:37.460 --> 00:09:40.810
and that pardon, rightfully,

00:09:40.810 --> 00:09:42.830
sparked bipartisan outrage.

00:09:42.830 --> 00:09:46.110
It sparked congressional inquiries.

00:09:46.110 --> 00:09:48.400
This is not to say that

00:09:48.400 --> 00:09:49.940
that particular pardon

00:09:49.940 --> 00:09:52.780
was, in any way, just or correct.

00:09:52.780 --> 00:09:55.163
People were rightly outraged about it.

00:09:56.320 --> 00:09:58.720
But this is so much worse.

00:09:58.720 --> 00:10:00.620
There was, and should have been,

00:10:00.620 --> 00:10:03.410
political fallout for that pardon.

00:10:03.410 --> 00:10:04.360
But what we're seeing

00:10:04.360 --> 00:10:05.560
out of the Trump administration

00:10:05.560 --> 00:10:08.490
is much, much worse.

00:10:08.490 --> 00:10:10.200
It's dozens of individuals

00:10:10.200 --> 00:10:13.500
who have a direct
connection to the president.

00:10:13.500 --> 00:10:15.250
And the pardons being used in a way

00:10:15.250 --> 00:10:18.770
that really does
undermine the rule of law.

00:10:18.770 --> 00:10:21.570
And that's not an exaggeration.

00:10:21.570 --> 00:10:23.770
Because it's going to change the way

00:10:23.770 --> 00:10:25.100
that political institutions

00:10:25.100 --> 00:10:26.770
use the pardon in the future.

00:10:26.770 --> 00:10:28.300
And it's not going to get better,

00:10:28.300 --> 00:10:30.340
unless there are real punishments.

00:10:30.340 --> 00:10:33.410
Now I may be your discount John Krasinski,

00:10:33.410 --> 00:10:34.830
but let me try it to give you

00:10:34.830 --> 00:10:36.210
some good news here.

00:10:36.210 --> 00:10:38.300
The first is that Paul Manafort

00:10:38.300 --> 00:10:40.190
is not going to get his townhouses

00:10:40.190 --> 00:10:42.360
or ostrich jackets back.

00:10:42.360 --> 00:10:44.040
Under ex parte Garland,

00:10:44.040 --> 00:10:46.330
A pardon does not restore
offices forfeited,

00:10:46.330 --> 00:10:48.470
or property, or interest vested in others

00:10:48.470 --> 00:10:51.610
in consequences of a
conviction and judgment.

00:10:51.610 --> 00:10:53.560
So at least the Mueller Investigation

00:10:53.560 --> 00:10:55.200
will still have turned a profit.

00:10:55.200 --> 00:10:56.660
You also probably know that

00:10:56.660 --> 00:10:58.710
these pardons don't really

00:10:58.710 --> 00:11:00.380
affect state law prosecutions,

00:11:00.380 --> 00:11:04.020
if there is indeed
state-based criminality.

00:11:04.020 --> 00:11:07.040
We know that there are
ongoing investigations,

00:11:07.040 --> 00:11:08.810
particularly in New York.

00:11:08.810 --> 00:11:13.560
But I counsel you, don't hero
worship the investigators.

00:11:13.560 --> 00:11:16.040
We've been burned time and time again.

00:11:16.040 --> 00:11:18.660
That sometimes that's
just too much pressure

00:11:18.660 --> 00:11:21.540
to put on people like
New York AG, Tish James

00:11:21.540 --> 00:11:23.700
and Manhattan DA, Cy Vance.

00:11:23.700 --> 00:11:24.750
A lot of the criminality

00:11:24.750 --> 00:11:27.060
that has been pardoned is purely federal

00:11:27.060 --> 00:11:30.770
with respect to lying
to federal prosecutors.

00:11:30.770 --> 00:11:34.300
With respect to federal
campaign finance violations

00:11:34.300 --> 00:11:35.853
and insider trading.

00:11:37.882 --> 00:11:40.280
It's unlikely that a lot of those crimes

00:11:40.280 --> 00:11:42.280
have state law counterparts that

00:11:43.170 --> 00:11:45.420
could even be investigated and punished,

00:11:45.420 --> 00:11:46.940
let alone will be.

00:11:46.940 --> 00:11:48.480
That being said,

00:11:48.480 --> 00:11:49.860
Paul Manafort was convicted

00:11:49.860 --> 00:11:51.680
of numerous different tax crimes.

00:11:51.680 --> 00:11:53.730
And it's likely that New York state

00:11:53.730 --> 00:11:57.780
has similar state law tax crimes

00:11:57.780 --> 00:11:58.940
that he could be charged with.

00:11:58.940 --> 00:12:01.840
And even better news,

00:12:01.840 --> 00:12:04.150
recently the New York legislature

00:12:04.150 --> 00:12:05.650
closed a pardon loophole

00:12:05.650 --> 00:12:07.650
that would have prevented prosecution

00:12:07.650 --> 00:12:09.740
of someone who receives a pardon

00:12:09.740 --> 00:12:13.380
when there is an ancillary
New York state law

00:12:13.380 --> 00:12:14.550
to prosecute them under.

00:12:14.550 --> 00:12:16.850
So while Paul Manafort was initially

00:12:16.850 --> 00:12:20.490
successful in appealing
his New York prosecutions,

00:12:20.490 --> 00:12:22.530
it's possible that now

00:12:22.530 --> 00:12:24.250
that New York has closed this loophole,

00:12:24.250 --> 00:12:25.350
that they can move forward

00:12:25.350 --> 00:12:28.050
with prosecuting him on state law crimes.

00:12:28.050 --> 00:12:29.000
It's an open question.

00:12:29.000 --> 00:12:31.720
We'll see what the New
York appellate courts hold.

00:12:31.720 --> 00:12:33.430
You've also likely heard a lot

00:12:33.430 --> 00:12:34.830
about the Fifth Amendment,

00:12:34.830 --> 00:12:36.430
with respect to being pardoned.

00:12:36.430 --> 00:12:38.110
And it is indeed true that

00:12:38.110 --> 00:12:40.090
receiving a presidential pardon,

00:12:40.090 --> 00:12:41.560
if you accept it,

00:12:41.560 --> 00:12:44.380
does limit the scope under which

00:12:44.380 --> 00:12:46.350
you can claim the Fifth
Amendment privilege

00:12:46.350 --> 00:12:47.940
against self-incrimination.

00:12:47.940 --> 00:12:50.320
But it's, unfortunately, not absolute.

00:12:50.320 --> 00:12:52.280
If you face state law liability,

00:12:52.280 --> 00:12:55.270
then you can still invoke the
Fifth Amendment privilege.

00:12:55.270 --> 00:12:56.814
So this will indeed help

00:12:56.814 --> 00:12:59.290
both prosecutors and investigators

00:12:59.290 --> 00:13:01.510
with respect to inquiries

00:13:01.510 --> 00:13:02.667
related to these pardons,

00:13:02.667 --> 00:13:04.130
and the underlying criminality.

00:13:04.130 --> 00:13:08.070
But it's not going to help
that much, unfortunately.

00:13:08.070 --> 00:13:10.240
Additionally, it's possible that

00:13:10.240 --> 00:13:13.290
the pardons themselves might be crimes.

00:13:13.290 --> 00:13:14.123
Maybe.

00:13:15.110 --> 00:13:16.510
I wouldn't put too much stock in this,

00:13:16.510 --> 00:13:18.530
but remember that I said
that President Trump

00:13:18.530 --> 00:13:19.880
is not going to face criminal

00:13:19.880 --> 00:13:21.130
prosecution for these pardons.

00:13:21.130 --> 00:13:23.400
Well, it's possible that he might.

00:13:23.400 --> 00:13:24.260
There's a slim chance,

00:13:24.260 --> 00:13:25.780
but it's possible.

00:13:25.780 --> 00:13:27.170
We've seen time and time again

00:13:27.170 --> 00:13:29.880
that these members of
the Trump administration,

00:13:29.880 --> 00:13:31.320
especially the ones who have been around

00:13:31.320 --> 00:13:32.640
since the beginning,

00:13:32.640 --> 00:13:34.180
are completely inept.

00:13:34.180 --> 00:13:35.950
The DOJ has already gotten wind

00:13:35.950 --> 00:13:38.790
of a pardon for purchase scheme

00:13:38.790 --> 00:13:40.790
related to Elliott Broidy.

00:13:40.790 --> 00:13:43.560
And it's possible that there is

00:13:43.560 --> 00:13:44.990
an explicit agreement

00:13:44.990 --> 00:13:47.190
between members of the
Trump administration

00:13:47.190 --> 00:13:48.540
and these pardons.

00:13:48.540 --> 00:13:51.290
It's possible that people did attempt

00:13:51.290 --> 00:13:53.950
or were successful at buying a pardon.

00:13:53.950 --> 00:13:55.260
You can look at the list of people

00:13:55.260 --> 00:13:56.093
who received pardons.

00:13:56.093 --> 00:13:59.490
And it's not just Republican cronies

00:13:59.490 --> 00:14:00.870
and Trump cronies,

00:14:00.870 --> 00:14:02.490
people who actually engaged

00:14:02.490 --> 00:14:04.560
in real criminality.

00:14:04.560 --> 00:14:05.950
But also those who engaged

00:14:05.950 --> 00:14:07.030
in real criminality

00:14:07.030 --> 00:14:08.780
and are also just very, very rich.

00:14:08.780 --> 00:14:10.180
People that don't necessarily fit

00:14:10.180 --> 00:14:11.760
into this category of people

00:14:11.760 --> 00:14:13.100
who are being rewarded

00:14:13.100 --> 00:14:16.210
by the president for their
service to the president.

00:14:16.210 --> 00:14:18.050
People who might have the means

00:14:18.050 --> 00:14:21.060
to actually buy a pardon.

00:14:21.060 --> 00:14:25.570
And if those explicit
agreements are out there,

00:14:25.570 --> 00:14:29.970
it's possible that the
agreement was memorialized

00:14:29.970 --> 00:14:31.870
and that emails or documents will leak

00:14:31.870 --> 00:14:35.930
that the attorney-client
privilege will be violated

00:14:35.930 --> 00:14:38.170
because of the crime/fraud exception.

00:14:38.170 --> 00:14:40.400
And someone might talk

00:14:40.400 --> 00:14:43.283
after Trump can't actually
pardon people anymore.

00:14:43.283 --> 00:14:47.160
If there is an actual, clear quid pro quo

00:14:47.160 --> 00:14:48.600
between President Trump

00:14:48.600 --> 00:14:50.630
or other members of his administration

00:14:50.630 --> 00:14:54.200
and the granting of a pardon,

00:14:54.200 --> 00:14:55.990
it could conceivably give rise

00:14:55.990 --> 00:14:57.630
to independent criminality

00:14:57.630 --> 00:14:59.400
and potential punishment.

00:14:59.400 --> 00:15:00.233
That's a big if.

00:15:01.800 --> 00:15:04.680
But hopefully, this ends the discussion

00:15:04.680 --> 00:15:06.770
about future prosecutions

00:15:06.770 --> 00:15:09.770
or at least future investigations.

00:15:09.770 --> 00:15:11.500
Past pardons have led

00:15:11.500 --> 00:15:13.870
to congressional investigations.

00:15:13.870 --> 00:15:18.810
And this one absolutely
needs investigations

00:15:18.810 --> 00:15:22.070
if not outright prosecutions.

00:15:22.070 --> 00:15:24.130
And if not prosecutions
on a federal level,

00:15:24.130 --> 00:15:28.160
then prosecutions on a state law level.

00:15:28.160 --> 00:15:31.920
And, hopefully, this
represents the absolute zenith

00:15:31.920 --> 00:15:33.343
of presidential power.

00:15:35.200 --> 00:15:36.800
At the moment,

00:15:36.800 --> 00:15:39.680
The president has never
been more powerful.

00:15:39.680 --> 00:15:41.700
The president receives
almost unchecked power

00:15:41.700 --> 00:15:43.370
with respect to executive power

00:15:43.370 --> 00:15:44.633
and executive privilege.

00:15:45.580 --> 00:15:48.970
But these actions are
so far beyond the pale

00:15:50.440 --> 00:15:52.740
that I hope it forces

00:15:54.030 --> 00:15:57.070
the citizens and members of Congress

00:15:57.070 --> 00:15:58.510
to actually act.

00:15:58.510 --> 00:16:00.890
To actually put some
real checks and balances,

00:16:00.890 --> 00:16:02.460
and to scale back some of the power

00:16:02.460 --> 00:16:04.987
that has been granted from Congress

00:16:04.987 --> 00:16:06.403
to the presidency.

00:16:07.240 --> 00:16:09.030
Make no mistake,

00:16:09.030 --> 00:16:10.703
this is a political Rubicon.

00:16:11.580 --> 00:16:15.480
This is every bit as bad as it appears.

00:16:15.480 --> 00:16:16.313
In some way,

00:16:16.313 --> 00:16:21.150
we're lucky that they've
been so ham-fisted about this

00:16:21.150 --> 00:16:22.340
because there's no hiding it.

00:16:22.340 --> 00:16:24.260
This isn't 4D chess.

00:16:24.260 --> 00:16:29.260
This is just plain
cronyism and corruption.

00:16:29.270 --> 00:16:31.620
And it's gonna get worse
before it gets better.

00:16:33.040 --> 00:16:35.090
Just don't let it wear you down.

00:16:35.090 --> 00:16:36.870
But Americans did their part

00:16:36.870 --> 00:16:38.310
and they voted overwhelmingly

00:16:38.310 --> 00:16:40.140
to send President Trump packing.

00:16:40.140 --> 00:16:41.400
We could be looking down the barrel

00:16:41.400 --> 00:16:42.540
of four more years of this,

00:16:42.540 --> 00:16:45.280
but luckily he will be leaving office.

00:16:45.280 --> 00:16:47.500
But there's one last thing to do

00:16:47.500 --> 00:16:48.830
which is that we must demand

00:16:48.830 --> 00:16:50.680
of the future administrations

00:16:50.680 --> 00:16:53.900
that they not let these
pardons go unchecked.

00:16:53.900 --> 00:16:55.300
That they cannot allow

00:16:55.300 --> 00:16:58.250
this criminality to go unchecked.

00:16:58.250 --> 00:17:00.030
We assume that the
president's pardon power

00:17:00.030 --> 00:17:01.540
is near universal,

00:17:01.540 --> 00:17:04.200
but so much of this is debating

00:17:04.200 --> 00:17:06.400
how many angels can dance
on the head of a pin.

00:17:06.400 --> 00:17:09.230
Presidential pardons have
rarely been challenged.

00:17:09.230 --> 00:17:10.630
We don't know what the Supreme Court

00:17:10.630 --> 00:17:13.740
would have said if the
Ford pardon of Nixon

00:17:13.740 --> 00:17:14.590
had been challenged,

00:17:14.590 --> 00:17:17.950
or the Iran-Contra pardons
had been challenged.

00:17:17.950 --> 00:17:19.400
And we don't know what a Supreme Court

00:17:19.400 --> 00:17:23.040
would do with these
current raft of pardons.

00:17:23.040 --> 00:17:24.740
And we don't know all of the information

00:17:24.740 --> 00:17:26.430
about these particular pardons.

00:17:26.430 --> 00:17:28.830
Was there an explicit quid pro quo?

00:17:28.830 --> 00:17:30.410
Is there independent criminality

00:17:30.410 --> 00:17:32.240
about these particular pardons?

00:17:32.240 --> 00:17:34.550
The American people have a right to know

00:17:34.550 --> 00:17:36.140
that particular information.

00:17:36.140 --> 00:17:37.980
Which is why we must demand

00:17:37.980 --> 00:17:39.130
that the next administration,

00:17:39.130 --> 00:17:40.670
either through the attorney general

00:17:40.670 --> 00:17:42.360
or a special prosecutor,

00:17:42.360 --> 00:17:45.780
investigate the issuance of these pardons.

00:17:45.780 --> 00:17:47.840
Investigate the underlying
criminality itself.

00:17:47.840 --> 00:17:50.463
If there is remaining
criminality out there,

00:17:51.610 --> 00:17:53.520
charge them, indict them.

00:17:53.520 --> 00:17:55.180
Test the sufficiency of the pardon,

00:17:55.180 --> 00:17:57.470
test the breadth of the pardons.

00:17:57.470 --> 00:18:00.230
And let's see what the
Supreme Court has to say.

00:18:00.230 --> 00:18:01.400
And if the Supreme Court

00:18:01.400 --> 00:18:03.340
upholds the use of these pardons,

00:18:03.340 --> 00:18:04.173
then so be it.

00:18:04.173 --> 00:18:06.070
We can demand a constitutional amendment

00:18:06.070 --> 00:18:07.390
or other congressional means

00:18:07.390 --> 00:18:08.970
to put limits on this power

00:18:08.970 --> 00:18:11.540
because that's what Americans deserve.

00:18:11.540 --> 00:18:14.130
We fought a war to throw
off the rule of a king.

00:18:14.130 --> 00:18:15.670
And these pardons come

00:18:15.670 --> 00:18:17.810
as close as Americans ever have

00:18:17.810 --> 00:18:19.620
to reverting back to tyranny.

00:18:19.620 --> 00:18:22.358
Because as bad as these pardons are,

